//? Title: Double Dabble: Actual Add-Three States, Decimal Carries and Checked Bit Widths
//? Subtitle: Thirteen by hand, the original eight conversions, exact capacity and measured nibble work
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given a binary integer, we want its decimal digits using a conversion
recurrence that can be built from shifts, comparisons and small constant
adds. Binary-coded decimal stores each decimal digit in a four-bit
nibble, so an ordinary binary shift needs a correction at decimal carry
boundaries. Double Dabble adds three before shifting every digit at
least five. We derive that correction, inspect actual states for 13 and
243, retain the original eight conversions and add the full uint64_t
boundary. Exact width capacity, measured nibble operations and deliberate
low-bit truncation separate the algorithm from formatting and hardware
timing claims. The canonical core now validates widths and provides
owned stage evidence and a checked inverse for unpacked BCD digits.
)

\toc

> Thirteen by hand: correct six before the last shift

Take binary 1101, with four requested input bits. The consumed prefixes
are 1,3,6,13. Just before the last bit, the padded BCD field contains
[0,6]. Correct six to nine, then shift in the final one bit. The units
nibble computes 2·9+1=19, producing low nibble three and carry one;
the tens nibble receives that carry. The final BCD field is [1,3].
Each digit has its own four-bit encoding: 0001 0011 represents the
BCD digits one and three. Formatting those digits produces text “13”.

The table and diagram below use actual snapshots from the shared
executing kernel. Leading zero nibbles remain in stage evidence so that
carry movement is visible; the final digit result removes that padding.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dabble_thirteen.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::double_dabble_trace(13,4);
  std::print("| consumed bits | next bit | before | corrected | after | prefix |\n| ---: | ---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.steps.size();++i) {
    const auto& s=t.steps[i];
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",i+1,s.input_bit,s.before,s.corrected,s.after,s.prefix);
  }
  const auto& s=t.steps.back();
  std::print("\nLast carry-outs {}; result {}; digit checks {}; corrections {}.\n",s.carry_out,t.digits,t.work.digit_checks,t.work.add3_corrections);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(82,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=3.7;box.height=1.2;box.font_size=23;
  d.node("before",{0,2},std::format("before: {} | {}\n{:04b} | {:04b}",s.before[0],s.before[1],s.before[0],s.before[1]),box)
   .node("corrected",{5.6,2},std::format("corrected: {} | {}\n{:04b} | {:04b}",s.corrected[0],s.corrected[1],s.corrected[0],s.corrected[1]),box)
   .node("after",{2.8,-.5},std::format("after: {} | {}\n{:04b} | {:04b}",s.after[0],s.after[1],s.after[0],s.after[1]),box)
   .edge("before","corrected","add 3")
   .edge("corrected","after","shift in 1")
   .text({2.8,3.35},"Last stage of 1101 → decimal digits 13",26)
   .text({2.8,-1.7},"Units carry one into the tens nibble",23)
   .save_svg("build/dabble_thirteen.svg");
}
```
