> Derive the add-three rule and the prefix invariant

Let d∈{0,…,9} be a valid decimal digit and c∈{0,1} its incoming
carry, or the next binary input bit at the units position. Decimal
doubling requires low digit (2d+c) mod 10 and carry floor((2d+c)/10).

If d<5, then 2d+c≤9: shifting the nibble needs no correction.
If d≥5, pre-add three. The shifted binary nibble becomes

\[
2(d+3)+c=2d+c+6=16+(2d+c-10).
\]

Its bit-four carry is one and its low four bits are exactly the desired
decimal remainder, between zero and nine. The threshold is still five
when c=1. This proves the local rule for all twenty digit/carry pairs.
Carry propagation runs from the units nibble toward the most significant.
Corrected intermediate nibbles may have values ten, eleven or twelve;
they are binary intermediate fields rather than valid decimal digits.

For the global invariant, let Pₖ be the selected binary prefix after k
bits. Initially P₀=0 and the BCD field is zero. Each next bit b gives
Pₖ₊₁=2Pₖ+b. The local correction makes the entire BCD field perform
this exact decimal doubling and incoming-bit addition. Induction proves
that every post-shift state encodes its consumed prefix, including the
final selected value. Capacity sufficient for the full requested width
also suffices for every prefix.

> Inspect all eight stages of 243

The original first input is 243, binary 11110011. Its prefixes are
1,3,7,15,30,60,121,243. The next table shows every actual correction
and outgoing carry. For example, prefix seven is corrected to nibble ten
before shifting in the fourth one bit. The post-shift field is again
valid BCD, representing fifteen. The heatmap retains all three requested-
width nibbles; the curve decodes the same post-shift states.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dabble_243.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::double_dabble_trace(243,8);
  std::vector<std::vector<double>> z(3,std::vector<double>(8));
  std::vector<double> stage,prefix,rows;
  std::vector<std::string> row_names;
  std::print("| stage | input | before | corrected | after | carry-outs | prefix |\n| ---: | ---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.steps.size();++i) {
    const auto& s=t.steps[i];
    if(dm::algorithms::bcd_to_uint64(s.after)!=s.prefix) throw std::runtime_error("prefix invariant failed");
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",i+1,s.input_bit,s.before,s.corrected,s.after,s.carry_out,s.prefix);
    stage.push_back(i+1);prefix.push_back(s.prefix);
    for(std::size_t j=0;j<3;++j) z[j][7-i]=s.after[j];
  }
  std::print("\nFinal decimal digits {}; string {}.\n",t.digits,dm::algorithms::double_dabble_string(243,8));
  for(int i=8;i>=1;--i) {rows.push_back(-i);row_names.push_back(std::to_string(i));}
  auto field=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  field.image({0,1,2},rows,z,{{239,246,255},{219,234,254},{191,219,254},{147,197,253},{96,165,250}},0,9);
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<8;++i) for(std::size_t j=0;j<3;++j)
    field.text(j,-static_cast<double>(i+1),std::to_string(t.steps[i].after[j]),{17,24,39},19);
  field.x_ticks({0,1,2},{"hundreds","tens","units"}).y_ticks(rows,row_names)
   .title("Actual post-shift BCD fields").x_label("decimal position").y_label("consumed bits");
  auto growth=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  growth.line(stage,prefix,"prefix",{37,99,235}).points(stage,prefix,"",{37,99,235},5)
   .title("Decoded consumed prefix").x_label("consumed bits").y_label("prefix value").y_limits(0,310);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(field).add(growth).size(1100,550)
   .title("11110011: every actual state satisfies the decimal-prefix invariant")
   .fit_panels().save_svg("build/dabble_243.svg");
}
