> Retain every original conversion and separate width from value

The original eight cases are retained, including zero and the full
32-bit value 4294967295. The final row adds UINT64_MAX,
18446744073709551615. The returned vector is unpacked BCD: one int
per decimal digit in most-significant-first order. It is not a vector
of bytes containing two packed BCD digits per byte.

For B>0 requested bits, the largest selected value is 2ᴮ−1 and the
required capacity is its decimal length,

\[
D(B)=\lfloor\log_{10}(2^B-1)\rfloor+1
=\lceil B\log_{10}2\rceil.
\]

For B=0, the API defines capacity one and result zero. The kernel uses
an exact fixed integer capacity table for widths zero through 64, with
no floating logarithm. A particular value can need fewer output digits
than that width's capacity. Zero requested at width eight returns one
digit while the fixed scratch field has three nibbles.

The original figure used requested bit width on its horizontal axis,
not the logarithm of the supplied value. The replacement labels it
explicitly and plots the exact capacity alongside individual examples;
several values can share a width and have different decimal lengths.
Each example also round-trips through the checked BCD decoder.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dabble_capacity.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> widths,capacity,example_width,example_length;
  std::print("| input value | requested bits | capacity | digits | decimal string | standard decimal | match |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n");
  for(const auto [value,bits]:std::vector<std::pair<std::uint64_t,int>>{{243,8},{0,8},{255,8},{1000,16},{65535,16},{123456,20},{1000000,20},{4294967295ULL,32},{std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max(),64}}) {
    const auto digits=dm::algorithms::double_dabble(value,bits);
    const auto text=dm::algorithms::double_dabble_string(value,bits);
    const auto expected=std::to_string(value);
    const bool match=text==expected && dm::algorithms::bcd_to_uint64(digits)==value;
    if(!match) throw std::runtime_error("conversion mismatch");
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",value,bits,dm::algorithms::double_dabble_capacity(bits),digits,text,expected,match);
    example_width.push_back(bits);example_length.push_back(text.size());
  }
  for(int b=0;b<=64;++b) {widths.push_back(b);capacity.push_back(dm::algorithms::double_dabble_capacity(b));}
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.line(widths,capacity,"capacity",{37,99,235})
   .points(example_width,example_length,"examples",{220,38,38},6)
   .title("Exact width capacity and individual decimal lengths")
   .x_label("requested binary width B").y_label("decimal digits")
   .y_limits(0,26).size(1100,570).save_svg("build/dabble_capacity.svg");
}
```
