> Count actual nibble work and state the computational model

This implementation examines and shifts all D allocated nibbles once
per requested input bit, including leading zeros. Its measured counts
therefore satisfy

\[
\text{digit checks}=\text{nibble shifts}=B\,D(B).
\]

Every corrected nibble produces one decimal carry, so the total number
of carries equals the total add-three corrections. Corrections depend
on the value; all-zero input performs no corrections but still visits
B·D nibbles. The next program checks those identities at every width
from zero through 64 and prints representative rows.

In a general B-bit version, D(B)=Θ(B), so this full-field software
loop takes Θ(B²) nibble operations and O(B) scratch space. Retaining
all before/corrected/after/carry snapshots takes O(B²) captured storage.
The public uint64_t domain bounds both: at most 64 stages and twenty
nibbles per snapshot. Work counters omit allocation, copies, formatting
and zero trimming; they are neither wall-clock measurements nor FPGA
cycle/area predictions. A hardware implementation may use parallel
correction cells or a differently scheduled circuit.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dabble_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> widths,visits,zero_corrections,one_corrections;
  std::print("| bits | nibbles | checks | shifts | zero corrections | all-one corrections | all-one carries |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(int b=0;b<=64;++b) {
    const auto zero=dm::algorithms::double_dabble_work(0,b);
    const auto ones=dm::algorithms::double_dabble_work(std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max(),b);
    const auto expected=static_cast<std::size_t>(b)*dm::algorithms::double_dabble_capacity(b);
    if(zero.digit_checks!=expected || ones.digit_checks!=expected || zero.nibble_shifts!=expected || ones.nibble_shifts!=expected || zero.add3_corrections || ones.add3_corrections!=ones.decimal_carries)
      throw std::runtime_error("work identity failed");
    if(b==0 || b==1 || b==4 || b==8 || b==16 || b==32 || b==64)
      std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",b,dm::algorithms::double_dabble_capacity(b),ones.digit_checks,ones.nibble_shifts,zero.add3_corrections,ones.add3_corrections,ones.decimal_carries);
    widths.push_back(b);visits.push_back(ones.nibble_shifts);
    zero_corrections.push_back(zero.add3_corrections);one_corrections.push_back(ones.add3_corrections);
  }
  auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  a.line(widths,visits,"checks=shifts",{37,99,235})
   .title("Both values visit every allocated nibble").x_label("requested bits B")
   .y_label("checks or nibble shifts = B × D(B)").y_limits(0,1600);
  auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  b.line(widths,one_corrections,"all ones",{220,38,38})
   .line(widths,zero_corrections,"all zeros",{37,99,235})
   .title("Corrections equal decimal carries").x_label("requested bits B")
   .y_label("add-three corrections").y_limits(0,one_corrections.back()*1.35+1);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,550)
   .title("Actual logical work; no runtime or hardware-cycle inference")
   .fit_panels().save_svg("build/dabble_work.svg");
}
```
