> Verification and practical scope

Native tests exhaust every 16-bit value against standard decimal
formatting and inverse round-trips. All 8,191 values across widths zero
through twelve also receive full stage certificates using independent
schoolbook decimal doubling, rather than replaying nibble corrections.
Seeded full-width controls exercise every width 0…64, ignored high bits,
zero/all-one fields, decimal and binary boundaries, uint64_t maximum,
input validation, decoder overflow priority and owned snapshots.

The report uses canonical numeric fixtures because this is a radix
conversion algorithm rather than a data-fitting method. Its invariant,
capacity and work counts apply to each selected binary field. The
software trace explains the circuit idea without claiming CPU speedups,
a particular FPGA clock count or packed-decimal interchange semantics.

> References

Hao Zheng's [Modeling of Combinational Circuits](https://cse.usf.edu/~haozheng/teach/cda4253/slides/vhdl-2.pdf),
University of South Florida, includes the Shift and Add-3 (Double-Dabble)
construction. The local correction identity and prefix proof above derive
its decimal-carry behavior. [Ameer Abdelhadi's parametric binary-to-BCD converter](https://github.com/AmeerAbdelhadi/Binary-to-BCD-Converter)
provides a primary hardware implementation; its circuit organization is
distinct from this measured full-field C++ loop. All width, zero, ownership,
validation and inverse contracts here describe the executed datamunge API.

